{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500371-v20-animalism-2-why-survival","id":1500371,"title":"[V20] Animalism 2 why Survival?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-22T07:58:10-08:00","id":1500371,"title":"[V20] Animalism 2 why Survival?","content":"Is there any plausible explanation why the roll for Animalism 2 is made on Survival and not on Animal Ken?<br /> <br /> I mean survival is about mainly surviving in the wilderness, while Animal Ken is specifically for handling animals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T10:35:26-08:00","id":1500378,"title":"","content":"Not really? It's not like the Ability picks have ever had terribly consistent or strict rationales behind them.<br /> <br /> The best I can manage is that Animalism 2 isn't actually about directly interacting with animals, but rather mystically interacting with your environment. But I'll acknowledge it's a weak explanation.<br /> <br /> The real reason is probably because the game designers generally try to mix up the Attributes and Abilities within a Discipline to make it take ~2 Attributes and ~3 Abilities to get maximum use out of it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T11:54:53-08:00","id":1500385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500371-v20-animalism-2-why-survival?p=1500378#post1500378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really? It's not like the Ability picks have ever had terribly consistent or strict rationales behind them.</div> </div> </div> </div>While not strictly perfect in logic, they've mostly got reasonable rationales to them. I'm particularly fond of obfuscate using subterfuge because they actually see you but you're tricking their brain into believing the lie that you're not there.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe Animal ken is interacting with animals, Survival is knowing where to find them. If you know where to call, it makes a little sense that you're more likely to be answered (slot magic in for the logic leaps here, since An2 is really you shouting from the same place and different levels of knowledge wouldn't effect a mundane action done the exact same way.<br /> <br /> Survival is equally applicable to the hobo lifestyle as it is a taiga forest or rocky badlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 12-23-2022, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T15:55:37-08:00","id":1500403,"title":"","content":"I think OOC that game writers want to limit how much one Ability is useful to any one Discipline so that players don't increase that ability just to excel in succeeding with that Discipline. They wanted to spread things out. So sometimes you get abilities that don't seem to make as much sense as others.<br /> <br /> All Abilities to a degree are very wide ranging. As a result, there isn't always a clear distinction between certain abilities. To accomplish certain tasks, one can argue in favor of this Ability or that one. As ST I often allow different players to use different trait combinations to accomplish the same thing provided it makes sense. Animal Ken is about knowledge of &quot;animal behavior patterns&quot; while Survival covers a wide variety of things including &quot;track prey&quot; and avoiding dangers caused by animals. So there is an overlap of some kind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500371-v20-animalism-2-why-survival?p=1500385#post1500385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Animalism is interacting with animals, Survival is knowing where to find them. If you know where to call, it makes a little sense that you're more likely to be answered (slot magic in for the logic leaps here, since An2 is really you shouting from the same place and different levels of knowledge wouldn't effect a mundane action done the exact same way.<br /> <br /> Survival is equally applicable to the hobo lifestyle as it is a taiga forest or rocky badlands.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is probably the best justification I could come up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-23T01:10:12-08:00","id":1500433,"title":"","content":"In V20, tracking and wilderness hunting is based on Survival, IIRC, so I always assumed that was why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-23T01:53:25-08:00","id":1500436,"title":"","content":"Survival has always covered tracking, knowing where to find/look for things in the wild, etc. If I'm not mistaken, this has always been the test for Animalism 2, or at the very least since 1996's Vampire The Dark Ages. I think it makes sense, as you're calling the animals you want to call and you know where to find them. Animal Ken is about dealing with the animals, so besides the design's preference to spread disciplines tests among different abilities, this one makes quite a bit of sense, actually, as others have already pointed out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-23T05:14:47-08:00","id":1500446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500371-v20-animalism-2-why-survival?p=1500403#post1500403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think OOC that game writers want to limit how much one Ability is useful to any one Discipline so that players don't increase that ability just to excel in succeeding with that Discipline. They wanted to spread things out. So sometimes you get abilities that don't seem to make as much sense as others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I'm not a fan of this design. For lot of disiciplin powers you need someting between 6 and 10 dice to get somewhat reliably a decent result.<br /> <br /> Having to invest into mutiple attributes and abilities to get that gets quite expensive, and it is not like Discipline powers are that cheap to begin with. Or like the character generation rules are that generous with attribute and ability points to begin with...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T13:33:29-08:00","id":1501568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500371-v20-animalism-2-why-survival#post1500371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any plausible explanation why the roll for Animalism 2 is made on Survival and not on Animal Ken?<br /> <br /> I mean survival is about mainly surviving in the wilderness, while Animal Ken is specifically for handling animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is clear and understandable that Survival being used for the calculation / roll of this Animalism Discipline Invocation / Power represents and indicates clearly that concepts, ideas, choices, activites, themes, and emotions associated with Survival Ability / Skill are definitely in tune and also related to this Discipline Power, to a considerable and significant extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}